Package: deseq2reports
Title: Modular DESeq2 Pipeline with Automated HTML Reports
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Miu Shing", family = "Hung", email = "matthewhungms@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-0412-4374"))
Description: A self-contained, modular pipeline for RNA-seq differential expression
    analysis built on DESeq2. Provides one-command entry points
    (run_deseq2_wald() / run_deseq2_lrt() / run_deseq2_deg()) that chain quality
    control, sample distance/PCA, differential expression (Wald contrasts,
    time-course LRT with degPatterns, or a precomputed merged DEG table),
    gene set enrichment or cluster ORA against MSigDB collections, WGCNA /
    TF-activity / VIPER (bcellViper) / STRING PPI / CSPA modules (declared as
    Imports so they install with the package), and a rendered HTML report --
    as well as standalone modular functions for each stage so that individual
    steps can be run, inspected, or substituted independently. All behaviour
    that analysts commonly need to change per-analysis (count filtering
    thresholds, batch correction method, LFC shrinkage estimator, significance
    thresholds, ranking metric, MSigDB collections, colour palettes) is exposed
    as explicit function arguments with validated defaults.
